< From September 27 to October 5, 2026, the 14.2 refinement work ran the preregistered studies PREREG16 to PREREG44 (with PREREG28b) against the 14.1 benchmark record. **No engine file, coefficient or default of the shipped 14.1 was changed by any of them, and 14.1 remains the release.** The work produced an adopted scoring convention (volume under C1, or C2 where tags allow), an adopted scorer revision (r2, from PREREG37 on), one regional NS candidate that passes its benchmark gates but has not cleared a Bakuzis grid (v141LTfi), and named failures that locate the remaining NS and QC errors. The QC height anchor track is closed with the shipped 0.111 kept for 14.2: a field tag anchor (1.242) corrects QC height increment on the benchmark and passes a top height gate on measured heights against the 10% FIA measurement quality objective for tree length, but it fails the published TOPHT gate and does not clear the Bakuzis QC grid (PREREG38 to PREREG41), and the earlier QC height gates built on row index pairs are corrected by an erratum (PREREG42). The origin of 0.111 is now traced: no record fits it, and it was set by hand from a July 2026 stand level top height diagnostic (PREREG43). A Bakuzis QC grid started from measured stand lists (PREREG44) does not clear 1.242 either, and its reported trajectories show that neither scalar gives a credible long run height path, which points 14.3 at the QC height increment form. Each gated verdict follows a decision rule fixed before any held out value was read, and the one post hoc step, the PREREG21 split of its survivor term, is declared as such in that RESULT.
